+# TA2-SE result-admission and scalar-reader source map
+
+Public source-only map at source base/head `9292844a46aa4ba46701c9bb45cd703f0862dee6`, branch `docs/poc-ta2-se-admission-map-20261024`. No tests/imports/computation, app/Store/runtime, or artifact payloads were opened. Accepted plan `b97296f43598fb9d2cff2473a4910dc9c1d999bb` and different critique `f41b34efed3d7e3fd08dac846e3fc5e8886d95f5` are read as bounded public text only.
+
+The accepted scalar is the fixed implemented V0/V1 point estimator across planned independent cohorts, for one frozen scenario/ordinal/cutoff and declared successful-pair set. The plan's prose calls the value `result.member[j].effect.mean`; the current app contract actually exposes a `CohortResult.patients` list. In source, use the manifest's patient identity/history binding to locate `patients[j].effect.mean`; do not assume a `member` field exists. The critique explicitly requires whole-cohort admission before scalar selection, all member/chain/estimand diagnostic gates, and discarding every partial member effect when a joint result fails.
+
+| Stage | Existing source entry points and contract | Actual gate / limitation |
+|---|---|---|
+| Restricted truth request admission | `contracts/runs/private.py:276-315`, `TruthRequest.registered_target`, rejects a request whose bindings exactly equal the registered restricted profile (`:303-306`); other requests must resolve registered cell/unit or analytic fixture. `private_v2.py:57-66` subclasses the v1 request/response types. `services/evaluator/restricted.py:1-4,22-60` is a file-only TA1 offline CLI and states its output is never an admitted `TruthResponse`. | The inspected canonical TruthRequest path refuses the restricted profile, and the existing TA1 CLI is not an admission route. Do not treat its JSON as admitted truth or as matched-SE evidence. This is a bounded source conclusion, not a claim that every possible external path was searched. |
+| Authenticated cohort request and owner reads | `services/foundation/app.py:836-866` uses session/ownership checks and an authenticated mutation receipt when previewing/submitting `/api/cohort-analyses`; `:868-873` authenticates and owns the requested patient before returning attempts. `services/foundation/cohort_analysis.py:55-83` documents the caller-owned transaction/authenticated scope and inserts the frozen attempt; `contracts/domain/cohort.py:48-67,69-94` requires exactly 12 distinct versions and a canonically sorted 12-member manifest. | These are existing user request/read routes, not the scalar-calibration reader. The V0/V1 request must be admitted through its exact approved cohort input tuple; no new route is needed to retrieve saved summaries. |
+| Whole result and artifact ingest | `services/foundation/analysis.py:328-367` (`ingest`) parses the `result.json`, checks every listed artifact is a simple basename, rejects duplicate/symlink/missing/oversize entries, and verifies each referenced file SHA-256 before acquiring the Store write lock. `:374-415` rechecks the claim and commits the frozen typed result. Cohort results go through `:397-401`, where the frozen input must satisfy `require_executable` and `cohort_analysis.validate_result`; `:426-435` applies the persisted claim deadline and stores result JSON/status. | This is the normal result/artifact admission boundary to complete before selecting any member scalar. The foundation verifies byte identity and required names; it does not parse posterior NPZ arrays on the host. Semantic worker/output checks remain in the reviewed worker and typed result gates, not a new host posterior parser. |
+| Whole CohortResult/member gates | `contracts/domain/cohort.py:196-246` defines `PatientEffect` and `CohortResult`: exactly 12 patient records, same ordered `(patient_id, history_sha256)` identities as the frozen manifest, matching estimand/manifest/source intent, no member effect when the joint status fails, and all members completed when joint completion is reported. `services/foundation/cohort_analysis.py:110-136` binds attempt/input/cohort/manifest/configuration/source set; for completed output it checks trusted execution binding, accepted joint fit diagnostics, and for every patient accepted integration, accepted effect MCMC diagnostics, and required patient-specific expected-effect artifact. `:133-135` adds shared bridge gates for borrowed V1. | This is the server-side whole-result validator. Member checks are joint, not independently selectable successes. `analysis.ingest` hashes artifacts before this validator; it does not select scalars during validation. |
+| Worker production and joint failure | `services/learner/cohort_worker.py:43-68` starts with all member effects absent and a joint result failed. `:130-144` obtains each expected-effect trace, checks integration and per-effect MCMC diagnostics, writes `patient-<hash>-expected-effect.npz`, and records mean/SD/interval/unit/kind in each member; only after the loop is the whole result marked completed. `:145-158` catches any failure, sets every member's effect to `None` with joint failure status, then validates the complete `CohortResult`. | Exact source demonstrates why a valid-looking earlier member file cannot be independently used after a later member or joint-gate failure. Worker emits `mean(effect)` from accepted chain/draw conditional expected effects; `sd` is a distinct field and is not the estimator-SE denominator. |
+| Stored scalar summary reader | `services/foundation/appointment.py:30-41,44-112`, `public_summary` redacts seeds/private paths/posterior fields and `checked_result(row)` parses stored JSON, rebinds it to frozen input/attempt/status/config/estimand/cohort/manifest, checks joint diagnostics, and returns the whole sanitized model dump. It explicitly relies on ingest for file checksum verification and does not reopen NPZ/NetCDF. `services/foundation/cohort_analysis.py:18-52` `view` adds current cohort/member freshness. `:138-157` `comparison` preserves the full patient list for a same-cohort V0/V1 pair after `services/foundation/analysis.py:443-459` checks completed owned attempts and `checked_result`. | No scalar-only reader/adapter was found in this bounded set. Existing safe boundary is the already-ingested whole result returned by `checked_result`, or its whole-cohort paired output via `comparison`; both return the complete member summary and metadata. A scalar reducer must consume the requested ID-matched `patients[*].effect.mean` only after that admission and must preserve all cohort/attempt failures and exact pair identities. |
+
+The minimum handoff to the Sol implementation is therefore the existing path `analysis.ingest` → `cohort_analysis.validate_result` → persisted typed `CohortResult` → `appointment.checked_result`/`cohort_analysis.comparison`. The current restricted truth request path does not admit TA2 restricted truth. This map confirms no scalar-only qualified reader in the inspected files; the bounded adapter question is where to take the member scalar after accepted stored JSON, while retaining whole-result gates. It does not assert any current fit/truth acceptance or add/change requirements.
