+# Independent TA2-SE-DEFINITION-01 statistical PLAN critique
+
+Disposition: **ready_for_bounded_source_preparation_plan_only** for exact candidate `23999df87f2e43729d43fa1f180fa422794772e3`, accepted base `9292844a46aa4ba46701c9bb45cd703f0862dee6`. No blocking finding. The proposed definition is a defensible explicit empirical study convention, with the qualifications below; it is not a theorem equating unspecified prior interpretations. This accepts the definition proposal for explicit canonical adoption/source preparation, not a populated binding, numerical truth, SOURCE/OP implementation, execution, fit/study/clinical acceptance. ROOT's canonical adoption and subsequent exact reviews remain separate.
+
+Assigned/effective model is gpt-6-astra/medium per ROOT metadata confirmation. Own root/head/clean verified; different author. No helpers, candidate edits, project imports/tests, scientific calculations, native operations, private/sealed data, historical truth rows, Store/SQLite, Docker/image/current-resource queries or execution authority.
+
+## Statistical judgment
+
+**The experiment is now specified rather than selected by artifact availability.** Fixed scenario/behavior/external-source convention, pre-outcome member ordinal, cutoff, complete independent12-member cohorts and paired V0/V1 inputs define the replication unit. `A(H,U)` explicitly denotes the implemented finite algorithm. Sample SD across independently generated cohort replications estimates the variability of this reported scalar under that experiment. It does not become SD of the conditional estimation error, same-history posterior uncertainty, a study-mean SE or an infinite-computation posterior-mean SE. The source `services/learner/cohort_worker.py:141–143` supports the selected scalar: mean of the accepted chain/draw expected-effect array, distinct from its SD, interval and predictive endpoint artifacts.
+
+This choice addresses the original ambiguity without asserting an impossible equivalence theorem. The empirical-SE terminology is consistent with the primary [Morris, White and Crowther tutorial, section5](https://discovery.ucl.ac.uk/id/eprint/10066118/1/2019%20-%20Morris%20-%20simulation%20studies%20tutorial%20-%20stat%20med.pdf): across-repetition estimator SD is distinct from Monte Carlo uncertainty of a reported performance measure. That paper does not validate this project's varying-conditional-target experiment or its 10% threshold. Those remain the explicit project-level decision reviewed here.
+
+**The varying target is handled honestly.** The plan retains member H*-conditional DGP truth while the learner may use cohort sharing. `Var(error)=Var(Y)+Var(theta)-2Cov(Y,theta)` correctly separates estimator spread from error spread. SD(Y) can be large because histories/targets vary even when errors are tiny; therefore it cannot itself establish fine RMSE accuracy, coverage or superiority. The proposal does not make that claim: absolute ceilings, required sensitivity/ambiguity reporting and unresolved conditioning/grid gates remain. Constant estimators produce zero SD even with diffuse posterior, and cannot be rescued by posterior spread. No learner truth, realized latent state, generation key, future outcome or different patient's artifact supplies this calibration.
+
+**Successful-pair selection is an explicit conditional performance population, not erased failures.** Conditioning on both configurations' accepted outputs can change the history distribution and method comparison. It is legitimate for the named successful-pair scale because selection is prespecified, does not use truth/effect/error/coverage and all failed attempts remain in denominators. It must never be advertised as unconditional/full-population estimator performance. Configuration-specific success samples require their own declared calibration and cannot silently borrow the paired scale. Implementation must enforce accepted whole CohortResult plus member/chain/estimand gates: current worker lines147–152 withdraw every member output after a joint failure, so an earlier partial member file is not an eligible Y. This follows the plan's all-existing-gates rule, not a new restriction or source repair.
+
+**Including fit RNG is coherent for the fixed implemented algorithm, but not a precision loophole.** With frozen seeds/distributions, diagnostics, numerical budgets and predeclared extension/failure rules, U is part of that algorithm's sampling distribution. Changing those settings creates a different calibration identity; it cannot increase a previously frozen epsilon. Passing existing diagnostic metadata is necessary and does not magically prove zero numerical bias. Separate per-fit numerical-error reporting, genuine artifact admission and all current gates must remain. No added arbitrary Monte Carlo subtraction or new seed-replication experiment is required by this plan. This acceptance does not approve weakening computational settings or using failed/noisy artifacts to raise the scale.
+
+**Three successful pairs supply only a provisional engineering estimate.** Sample SD is not unbiased for SD or a lower confidence bound. Three to eight cohorts cannot guarantee a reliable population precision ratio; even final30–100 planned cohorts may yield sparse paired successes. The plan states these limits, reports actual counts and SD variability, treats inadequate cells as pending/inconclusive and retains all attempts. Its delete-one-cohort jackknife is a scalar diagnostic, not a confidence guarantee or a replacement denominator. It should not be used to claim calibrated coverage, a precise population SE, or permission to replace failed cohorts. No new fits solely to estimate this diagnostic are warranted.
+
+**Final-only tightening is appropriate prespecified numerical quality control.** The minimum of pilot, confirmation and earlier smaller accepted matching scales cannot relax the target. Freeze stratum/selection/aggregation and confirmation design before collection; do not repeatedly inspect results to choose a favorable success sample, settings, cutoff or stopping rule. Confirmation can require reevaluation/refinement of truth under a new reviewed operation, but cannot rewrite historical null fields or increase numerical budgets automatically. This is not model tuning or a claim that using the same calibration sample yields a deterministic bound on population SD. Zero/nonfinite/missing/mismatched scales remain unresolved or analytic-only.
+
+## Sensitivity, adequacy and remaining admission gates
+
+The algebraic sensitivity statements are correct for their stated premise of an independently justified per-pair bound `|theta_tilde-theta|<=epsilon`: empirical bias perturbation is bounded by mean epsilon, RMSE perturbation by its root-mean-square, and the paired **mean error difference** cancels a common truth value on identical scored pairs. Squared-error differences and separate RMSEs do not cancel. Coverage/sign/ranking classifications need endpoint/boundary ambiguity accounting. The report must use exactly the same pair set, weights and truth realization for any cancellation claim; unequal success subsets do not qualify.
+
